\label{lem:normalise-weights}
Each \(L_i\) has a linearisation whose fibre weights are
\refstepcounter{equation}

\[
\tag{\theequation}
\label{eq:normalised-weights}
\mu_{L_i}(p_I)=-\mathbf 1_{\{i\in I\}}.
\]

\label{lem:degree-weight}
For a linearised line bundle \(L\) on \(X\),
\refstepcounter{equation}

\[
\tag{\theequation}
\label{eq:degree-weight}
L\cdot C=\mu_L(p)-\mu_L(q).
\]

In particular, \(p\ne q\).
